WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:20.001
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:20.271 --> 01:22.396
Don't hurt me.

3
01:24.230 --> 01:29.230
I won't hurt you, but the Phii Pong is coming for you.

4
03:38.605 --> 03:42.896
DELUSION

5
04:24.063 --> 04:27.521
Have you ever lived in another nearby province?

6
04:27.605 --> 04:30.980
No, I've lived here all my life.

7
04:34.563 --> 04:37.271
Before you became a shaman,

8
04:38.230 --> 04:39.688
what did you do?

9
04:40.271 --> 04:43.271
Or have you been a ghost hunter since you were a kid?

10
04:47.688 --> 04:51.355
Back then, I lived at Narong's place.

11
04:52.396 --> 04:54.188
I helped Nee look after the field.

12
04:54.271 --> 04:56.021
She couldn't do it alone.

13
04:57.563 --> 05:03.688
I quit when the ancestral spirits called me to become a spirit medium.

14
05:06.355 --> 05:09.938
The ghost in our village is a Phii Pong, isn't it?

15
05:10.938 --> 05:13.313
Normally, doesn't it leave people alone?

16
05:14.896 --> 05:17.521
Unless someone sees its face.

17
05:17.605 --> 05:19.980
And if it knows someone has seen it,

18
05:20.063 --> 05:22.855
it'll throw banana leaves beside their house.

19
05:23.355 --> 05:25.105
Then someone in that house will die.

20
05:27.063 --> 05:32.230
There are plenty of ghosts that can kill people.

21
05:33.146 --> 05:34.271
The Pob.

22
05:34.771 --> 05:36.105
The Grasue.

23
05:36.730 --> 05:38.480
They're all over Isan.

24
05:39.730 --> 05:41.063
Spirit medium.

25
05:41.146 --> 05:42.438
Shaman.

26
05:43.105 --> 05:44.730
They're in every village.

27
05:45.438 --> 05:48.230
But this ghost we're hunting…

28
05:48.771 --> 05:49.855
Wow.

29
05:50.980 --> 05:53.646
It's far more brutal than anything I've ever read about.

30
05:54.563 --> 05:56.646
The victims…

31
05:57.480 --> 05:59.646
It feels more like a person did this.

32
06:06.563 --> 06:09.563
So is it really a Phii Pong, or something else?

33
06:09.646 --> 06:12.063
And even if it really is a ghost,

34
06:12.146 --> 06:15.521
would a ghost kill people the exact same way every single time?

35
06:20.563 --> 06:22.105
Well, that's food for thought.

36
06:23.313 --> 06:25.521
If a ghost wants us dead,

37
06:26.396 --> 06:28.021
it doesn't matter how it kills us.

38
06:28.105 --> 06:30.771
Dead is dead, Inspector.

39
06:34.980 --> 06:37.980
The villagers will come for the Rite of Calling the Kwan soon.

40
06:38.521 --> 06:40.063
Let's call it a day.

41
06:43.105 --> 06:44.730
Then I'll stop bothering you.

42
06:46.438 --> 06:48.063
There's one more thing, sir.

43
06:48.730 --> 06:51.896
You said you used to help Pannee in the field, right?

44
06:54.063 --> 06:56.563
There's a hut out in the woods.

45
06:57.480 --> 06:58.771
Who does it belong to?

46
07:03.021 --> 07:05.230
It's been there for a long time.

47
07:06.105 --> 07:08.646
I don't know who owns it.

48
07:12.813 --> 07:14.021
Then I'll be on my way.

49
08:43.771 --> 08:44.980
Aim.

50
08:45.063 --> 08:46.063
Yes?

51
08:46.646 --> 08:48.980
Doesn't your dad ever take you home?

52
08:51.688 --> 08:53.146
I'm bored, Mom.

53
08:53.646 --> 08:55.646
Grandma's house is so crowded.

54
08:56.146 --> 08:58.021
I don't like it.

55
08:58.105 --> 08:59.646
I want to go home.

56
09:00.146 --> 09:01.730
Come pick me up, Mom.

57
09:03.688 --> 09:05.396
I want to.

58
09:06.730 --> 09:08.813
But Grandpa is still unwell.

59
09:09.813 --> 09:11.438
Just wait a little longer, okay?

60
09:12.230 --> 09:13.980
I miss you so much.

61
09:17.563 --> 09:19.563
Where's your dad taking you?

62
09:19.646 --> 09:20.563
Why…

63
09:21.105 --> 09:23.146
Why is your suitcase out?

64
09:23.646 --> 09:24.688
Huh?

65
09:25.438 --> 09:30.146
Grandma wants to send me to live with Uncle in Bangkok.

66
09:31.146 --> 09:33.021
She showed me the school.

67
09:33.105 --> 09:34.355
Really?

68
09:35.730 --> 09:38.396
What did your dad say about that?

69
09:38.480 --> 09:40.563
He's going too.

70
09:40.646 --> 09:42.980
What about you, Mom? Are you coming?

71
09:43.063 --> 09:47.063
If you're not, I don't want to go.

72
09:49.605 --> 09:50.938
Don't worry.

73
09:51.730 --> 09:53.438
I won't let anyone

74
09:54.188 --> 09:56.105
take you far away from me.

75
09:58.938 --> 10:00.105
See you, dear.

76
10:00.646 --> 10:01.521
Bye.

77
10:25.771 --> 10:27.271
Mrs. Wanrudee Kudprathum?

78
10:30.605 --> 10:32.730
My name is Supattra Mettayakul.

79
10:32.813 --> 10:35.438
I'm the attorney appointed by Mr. Yote Choketanagoon.

80
10:37.313 --> 10:38.480
Here are the documents.

81
10:43.105 --> 10:45.646
Please take your time and read them carefully.

82
10:45.730 --> 10:48.771
I've been instructed to inform you that

83
10:48.855 --> 10:51.771
Mr. Yote is willing to divide the marital assets.

84
10:51.855 --> 10:55.813
As for the custody of your son, Aimyote Choketanagoon,

85
10:55.896 --> 10:57.730
Mr. Yote is seeking sole custody.

86
10:57.813 --> 10:59.896
Go back and tell your client

87
11:00.938 --> 11:02.938
that he's never getting our son.

88
11:04.396 --> 11:05.938
And as for the divorce,

89
11:06.021 --> 11:07.688
it won't be as easy as he thinks.

90
11:10.438 --> 11:11.730
Understood.

91
11:12.230 --> 11:14.980
Mr. Yote will file for divorce immediately.

92
11:15.063 --> 11:17.188
You're free to appoint your own attorney.

93
11:18.438 --> 11:20.771
The next step will be mediation.

94
11:20.855 --> 11:23.730
My task here is done.

95
11:23.813 --> 11:25.313
I'll leave now.

96
11:41.396 --> 11:42.646
This was prescribed ages ago.

97
11:43.230 --> 11:44.938
Why is there still so much left, Mom?

98
11:46.105 --> 11:48.063
It depends on your father's mood.

99
11:48.646 --> 11:50.730
Some days he takes it. Some days he doesn't.

100
11:50.813 --> 11:51.896
What am I supposed to do?

101
11:52.688 --> 11:53.896
No, Mom.

102
11:54.396 --> 11:55.980
He has to take it consistently.

103
11:56.063 --> 11:57.730
Otherwise, he'll have an episode.

104
11:57.813 --> 11:59.438
He only listens to Wan.

105
11:59.521 --> 12:01.105
Look around.

106
12:01.188 --> 12:02.063
Is she even here?

107
12:03.771 --> 12:05.730
Things at her place are a mess.

108
12:05.813 --> 12:06.896
Don't nag her, Mom.

109
12:09.021 --> 12:11.480
It's fine if he misses a few doses.

110
12:11.980 --> 12:14.146
But at least he never misses his holy water.

111
12:15.896 --> 12:17.271
Okay, fine.

112
12:20.771 --> 12:22.063
Come on, Dad.

113
12:22.146 --> 12:25.271
Take this vitamin. It'll help keep you healthy.

114
12:25.355 --> 12:27.771
No. No!

115
12:27.855 --> 12:29.188
I'm not crazy.

116
12:30.146 --> 12:32.021
Don't try to trick me into taking pills.

117
12:32.105 --> 12:34.438
If you want them, you take them yourselves.

118
12:35.230 --> 12:37.980
It's just a vitamin, Dad. Not medicine.

119
12:39.230 --> 12:40.730
Just one pill.

120
12:41.730 --> 12:42.563
Here.

121
12:43.813 --> 12:45.605
-Please. -You're the crazy ones.

122
12:46.230 --> 12:48.105
None of you believe a word I say.

123
12:49.355 --> 12:51.480
There are ghosts in the forest.

124
12:52.188 --> 12:55.146
They'll eat you, one by one.

125
13:05.646 --> 13:10.230
LOEI CCTV SHOP

126
13:14.271 --> 13:16.063
-Looking for a security camera, ma'am? -Huh?

127
13:17.313 --> 13:19.021
-Yes. -What do you need it for?

128
13:19.105 --> 13:20.771
Well…

129
13:21.396 --> 13:24.313
to keep an eye on the elderly at home, in case of an emergency.

130
13:32.105 --> 13:33.021
This one should do.

131
13:33.105 --> 13:34.980
It has plenty of built-in storage.

132
13:35.063 --> 13:36.688
No need to change the memory card often.

133
13:37.855 --> 13:40.438
LOEI RATCHANAKHARIN PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

134
13:40.521 --> 13:41.605
No, I won't go.

135
13:41.688 --> 13:43.771
I won't. I'm not crazy.

136
13:43.855 --> 13:45.021
Ouch.

137
13:45.105 --> 13:45.938
Let's go.

138
13:46.438 --> 13:49.563
The patient is stubborn about taking his medication, I take it?

139
13:51.355 --> 13:52.188
Yes.

140
13:52.855 --> 13:57.563
In that case, the hallucinations and mood swings will probably come back.

141
13:59.355 --> 14:01.146
Actually, his condition does improve

142
14:01.688 --> 14:03.688
when we can get him to take his medication.

143
14:05.230 --> 14:07.146
Then how about trying a patch this time?

144
14:07.230 --> 14:08.813
It might be a little easier.

145
14:08.896 --> 14:11.313
Something like a medicated patch.

146
14:11.396 --> 14:12.271
And…

147
14:12.355 --> 14:16.271
does risperidone come in a liquid form?

148
14:16.938 --> 14:19.730
I think it'd be easier to slip it into a drink.

149
14:20.980 --> 14:23.146
Like pretending it's holy water.

150
14:25.438 --> 14:30.230
This time, I'll prescribe the equivalent of the remaining pills' dosage.

151
14:30.313 --> 14:33.980
It'd be good if you could bring the patient in next time.

152
14:34.063 --> 14:36.355
Will do, thank you.

153
14:46.521 --> 14:48.438
Thank you for taking the time to be here today.

154
14:49.146 --> 14:51.896
Has Mrs. Wanrudee reviewed all the documents?

155
14:51.980 --> 14:52.813
Yes.

156
14:53.813 --> 14:54.813
Good.

157
14:54.896 --> 14:59.063
In that case, we'll begin with the child custody arrangement

158
14:59.146 --> 15:02.105
for Aimyote Choketanagoon.

159
15:02.188 --> 15:03.063
Yes.

160
15:04.063 --> 15:06.480
Aren't we starting with the divorce petition?

161
15:07.105 --> 15:08.688
And where's your client?

162
15:14.605 --> 15:16.271
What have I missed?

163
15:19.688 --> 15:21.188
Aim must live with me.

164
15:23.688 --> 15:25.938
How can you take him away and raise him alone?

165
15:26.438 --> 15:29.521
Whenever you and your mom want to show Aim off, come pick him up.

166
15:32.188 --> 15:36.771
I believe that, if Mr. Yote wanted to discuss custody,

167
15:36.855 --> 15:37.896
he should've informed us.

168
15:37.980 --> 15:43.021
Because after the divorce is finalized, the law grants custody to the mother.

169
15:48.688 --> 15:50.646
Did she ever tell you…

170
15:54.396 --> 15:55.688
that her father

171
15:57.063 --> 15:58.980
once took Aim into the forest,

172
16:00.021 --> 16:01.313
and he almost died?

173
16:02.521 --> 16:06.688
Mr. Yote and his family have cause to question Aim's safety.

174
16:07.521 --> 16:09.855
Aim told Mr. Yote

175
16:10.355 --> 16:12.355
everything that happened in the forest.

176
16:13.980 --> 16:16.271
If that turns out to be true,

177
16:17.855 --> 16:20.605
it could constitute a criminal offense that's a non-compoundable offense.

178
16:21.938 --> 16:25.271
Dementia can't be one hundred percent controlled.

179
16:25.896 --> 16:27.396
You can't be

180
16:27.480 --> 16:30.271
with your son

181
16:30.355 --> 16:32.230
or your sick father at all times.

182
16:33.480 --> 16:34.438
Isn't that right?

183
16:37.355 --> 16:39.313
Aim must stay with me.

184
16:45.230 --> 16:46.855
If you want to make this a big deal…

185
16:49.771 --> 16:51.105
then we'll settle it in court.

186
16:59.938 --> 17:02.396
-Wow, the food here is good. -Yes.

187
17:03.480 --> 17:05.855
Here, sit down.

188
17:06.980 --> 17:07.813
Okay.

189
17:08.980 --> 17:13.313
The 30,000 you asked me for to keep your repair shop afloat…

190
17:13.396 --> 17:14.855
I got it.

191
17:17.355 --> 17:18.813
Here.

192
17:20.771 --> 17:22.313
Thank you so much.

193
17:22.396 --> 17:26.105
Just don't forget to pay me back with interest.

194
17:26.688 --> 17:28.105
If you don't,

195
17:28.938 --> 17:31.146
I'll send a ghost after you.

196
17:32.688 --> 17:33.646
Come on.

197
17:34.146 --> 17:35.605
I wouldn't dare.

198
17:36.480 --> 17:38.855
I'm already grateful you lent it to me.

199
17:38.938 --> 17:40.813
This round of drinks is on me.

200
17:40.896 --> 17:42.188
Come on.

201
17:42.271 --> 17:43.646
There's no need.

202
17:44.771 --> 17:47.355
Go ahead and order whatever you guys want.

203
17:47.438 --> 17:49.063
This meal is on me.

204
17:50.813 --> 17:53.563
Go. Get some more booze.

205
17:53.646 --> 17:55.063
You stick with me,

206
17:55.146 --> 17:57.313
and you'll always have food on the table.

207
17:57.855 --> 18:00.646
You'll be living even better than this. Mark my words.

208
18:01.938 --> 18:02.771
Let's drink.

209
18:02.855 --> 18:04.605
Cheers.

210
18:05.105 --> 18:07.313
-Drink up. -Nice.

211
18:07.396 --> 18:08.480
-Sir? -Yeah?

212
18:08.563 --> 18:09.396
Drink.

213
18:09.938 --> 18:11.230
Slowly, Dad.

214
18:11.980 --> 18:14.688
Slowly, there's no need to rush.

215
18:18.646 --> 18:20.396
Get your father some water.

216
18:38.438 --> 18:39.313
What is that?

217
18:44.188 --> 18:45.563
Liquid medicine.

218
18:47.938 --> 18:49.730
Is it better than the old one?

219
18:50.480 --> 18:52.271
It's easier to take.

220
18:52.980 --> 18:55.855
And look, you can mix it with your holy water.

221
18:55.938 --> 18:58.230
That way, he'll be treated both ways.

222
19:01.063 --> 19:04.021
It's not that I don't believe the doctors know what they're doing.

223
19:05.355 --> 19:07.605
But on the days he doesn't take his medicine,

224
19:07.688 --> 19:09.563
he still seems to get better.

225
19:09.646 --> 19:11.813
These medications take time, Mom.

226
19:12.313 --> 19:16.188
It's like fever medicine. One pill doesn't cure you right away.

227
19:18.271 --> 19:19.771
Here, Dad.

228
19:20.396 --> 19:21.605
Have some water.

229
19:36.938 --> 19:39.855
Hey, I'm going to head home.

230
19:39.938 --> 19:41.521
I'm getting tipsy.

231
19:42.521 --> 19:44.980
I'm afraid I'll crash on the way.

232
19:46.813 --> 19:48.063
Drive safe.

233
19:51.396 --> 19:52.730
Old car, old man…

234
19:52.813 --> 19:54.396
neither starts when you expect them to.

235
19:56.855 --> 19:57.730
Getting old, huh?

236
19:58.230 --> 19:59.688
See you around.

237
20:41.396 --> 20:45.938
You'll need to pay half of the legal fees up front.

238
20:46.021 --> 20:49.396
Does that fee guarantee we'll win the case?

239
20:49.980 --> 20:52.188
Well… that's hard to say.

240
20:53.105 --> 20:55.855
Cases like this usually take quite a long time.

241
20:56.563 --> 20:57.980
Even if we win,

242
20:58.063 --> 21:01.855
the other party can still file an appeal within the legal deadline.

243
21:02.355 --> 21:05.021
So this won't end at just one court appearance?

244
21:05.771 --> 21:06.813
And…

245
21:06.896 --> 21:11.896
do I have to keep hiring a lawyer for each stage of the case?

246
21:11.980 --> 21:13.146
Yes.

247
21:13.230 --> 21:14.896
But judging by the other side,

248
21:14.980 --> 21:18.521
this will go through several hearings before it's finally settled.

249
21:19.605 --> 21:23.938
If you can't keep fighting this, I think another mediation would be better.

250
21:28.688 --> 21:31.146
Vice Principal Wan, are you free?

251
21:31.230 --> 21:32.688
I'd like to talk to you.

252
21:33.313 --> 21:34.605
Please, come in.

253
21:34.688 --> 21:36.688
I'll call you back.

254
21:49.480 --> 21:50.480
How's your father?

255
21:51.855 --> 21:53.271
Is he any better?

256
21:55.188 --> 21:56.563
He's doing better.

257
22:03.063 --> 22:03.938
Vice Principal Wan.

258
22:04.813 --> 22:08.146
Actually, should you go clear this and that so that it's done first?

259
22:08.855 --> 22:11.980
If anything comes up, I'll send the documents over for your signature.

260
22:14.105 --> 22:18.105
Is my personal life causing problems for the school?

261
22:18.646 --> 22:21.563
It's not that I have a problem, but…

262
22:22.480 --> 22:24.313
quite a few parents

263
22:25.021 --> 22:27.646
are uneasy about the rumors surrounding your father.

264
22:28.271 --> 22:31.063
And the victim was about the same age as our students.

265
22:32.563 --> 22:34.688
People are worried.

266
22:37.813 --> 22:38.646
It's just that…

267
22:40.271 --> 22:42.438
my father is sick.

268
22:44.938 --> 22:46.813
He has dementia.

269
22:48.230 --> 22:49.646
He didn't kill anyone.

270
22:50.855 --> 22:52.605
I can assure you of that.

271
22:54.605 --> 22:56.355
I understand.

272
22:57.730 --> 22:59.480
It's not that I don't believe you.

273
23:01.438 --> 23:03.313
But please do as I suggested.

274
23:04.021 --> 23:04.896
Trust me.

275
23:22.188 --> 23:23.271
Here, sir.

276
23:35.188 --> 23:37.271
I can't approve it, Inspector.

277
23:40.771 --> 23:44.396
I don't see how it's connected to the current case we're working on.

278
23:44.480 --> 23:46.480
How is it not connected, sir?

279
23:46.563 --> 23:49.813
Sak only started becoming a shaman and gaining the villagers' trust

280
23:49.896 --> 23:53.105
after the murder of Thongdee's son over ten years ago.

281
23:53.188 --> 23:56.105
I think there are many suspicious things here, sir.

282
23:57.813 --> 23:59.521
And what exactly

283
24:00.230 --> 24:01.688
do you find suspicious?

284
24:02.730 --> 24:05.230
Sak stands to benefit from the bodies the most.

285
24:05.730 --> 24:09.688
When someone dies, people get scared and more people go to Sak for help.

286
24:11.105 --> 24:14.480
What evidence do we have to accuse him, kid?

287
24:17.563 --> 24:18.688
Listen to me.

288
24:20.813 --> 24:22.646
You're not from here.

289
24:24.980 --> 24:27.146
So let me give you some advice.

290
24:28.188 --> 24:30.396
If you raid the spirit medium's house,

291
24:31.313 --> 24:33.771
you represent all of us officers.

292
24:34.896 --> 24:37.396
You'll be seen as offending someone the villagers respect.

293
24:38.771 --> 24:40.730
And you'll be working here for a long time.

294
24:41.730 --> 24:44.146
How are you supposed to keep doing your job?

295
24:46.396 --> 24:48.313
So I won't approve it.

296
24:49.396 --> 24:50.730
Understood, sir.

297
24:53.730 --> 24:56.521
I think you'd be better off finding a new basis for the investigation.

298
25:04.771 --> 25:08.146
KAENG KHUT KHU

299
25:36.771 --> 25:41.563
YOU CAN WIRE ME THE MONEY THAT YOU WERE GOING TO LEND MOM

300
25:53.730 --> 25:57.230
You're a civil servant. Can you really drink in public like this?

301
26:04.896 --> 26:07.063
I might not be for much longer.

302
26:09.313 --> 26:11.646
Not while my father is still a suspect.

303
26:16.646 --> 26:18.688
Is there something you want to ask me, Inspector?

304
26:25.063 --> 26:27.896
Has your family ever had any conflict with the shaman named Sak?

305
26:29.396 --> 26:31.105
Isn't he Pannee's older brother?

306
26:31.980 --> 26:33.730
Why does it seem like you aren't close?

307
26:35.355 --> 26:38.313
He used to help out at your family's place, didn't he?

308
26:41.063 --> 26:42.563
They probably had a falling out…

309
26:46.605 --> 26:48.438
because of money.

310
26:51.230 --> 26:53.771
When Narong caused a scene at the hospital,

311
26:53.855 --> 26:57.021
he was worried that your mother would steal his money for your uncle Sak.

312
26:57.105 --> 26:58.021
Is that right?

313
27:01.230 --> 27:03.730
But my father's words aren't exactly reliable.

314
27:04.813 --> 27:06.688
It's fifty-fifty.

315
27:06.771 --> 27:09.063
People with dementia who ramble like that

316
27:09.146 --> 27:11.563
are usually recalling memories from the past.

317
27:13.146 --> 27:14.355
It's interesting.

318
27:22.563 --> 27:24.313
So what does Uncle Sak have to do with it?

319
27:25.063 --> 27:29.188
I think your uncle Sak is more of a suspect than your father.

320
27:30.105 --> 27:31.313
How so?

321
27:32.271 --> 27:33.813
I can't say much right now.

322
27:34.521 --> 27:36.230
It could affect the investigation.

323
27:37.521 --> 27:38.980
Anything else?

324
27:40.063 --> 27:41.021
I'm leaving.

325
27:42.230 --> 27:46.021
But I think I can help clear your father's name.

326
27:48.605 --> 27:50.230
I just need a little favor.

327
27:57.063 --> 27:58.813
The DNA results are back.

328
27:58.896 --> 28:02.063
The hair found on Mued's body doesn't belong to your father.

329
28:02.146 --> 28:03.980
You can stop worrying.

330
28:04.563 --> 28:07.771
But the villagers will still think your dad is the Phii Pong.

331
28:07.855 --> 28:11.146
So, I want your uncle Sak's DNA for cross-reference.

332
28:13.230 --> 28:16.105
But with how things work in our system, that's not easy, is it?

333
28:21.188 --> 28:22.980
So I'd like your help.

334
28:25.938 --> 28:28.396
I think it's a win-win situation.

335
28:28.480 --> 28:30.271
I catch the real culprit,

336
28:31.230 --> 28:32.813
and your family is off the hook.

337
28:34.855 --> 28:36.105
Interested?

338
28:44.188 --> 28:46.230
And now, our next story.

339
28:46.313 --> 28:51.771
A murder case in Na Sao Village in Loei.

340
28:51.855 --> 28:53.605
After the murder,

341
28:53.688 --> 28:57.688
rumors spread that it was the work of a Phii Pong.

342
28:57.771 --> 28:59.063
This case

343
28:59.146 --> 29:04.646
closely resembles one that happened in the same area over ten years ago.

344
29:04.730 --> 29:06.730
The villagers have all…

345
29:40.271 --> 29:42.521
Sak and the others are out drinking right now.

346
29:42.605 --> 29:45.063
This is our chance to sneak in and look for evidence.

347
29:53.813 --> 29:55.605
We must break into his house.

348
29:57.188 --> 29:59.813
I'm a police officer. I refuse to break the law.

349
30:15.188 --> 30:16.521
Careful.

350
30:28.438 --> 30:31.188
When the system can't be relied on, this is what it comes to.

351
30:32.105 --> 30:33.730
You can stay here, Officer.

352
30:33.813 --> 30:35.896
If anyone sees us, just arrest me.

353
31:05.771 --> 31:07.646
If you're coming in, go around to the front.

354
31:34.021 --> 31:36.896
Cigarette butts, hair, fingernails. Anything, right?

355
31:39.063 --> 31:39.938
Hey.

356
31:41.730 --> 31:43.063
Put gloves on first.

357
33:05.438 --> 33:07.063
Hey, stay down there.

358
33:07.146 --> 33:09.855
I'll be down in a minute.

359
33:16.188 --> 33:18.396
Hey, what the hell?

360
33:41.771 --> 33:43.980
Hey! Come out!

361
33:44.896 --> 33:46.271
Or I'll shoot!

362
35:05.896 --> 35:07.021
What's going on?

363
35:07.938 --> 35:08.980
Damn it.

364
35:09.063 --> 35:11.896
You could've made some noise. You scared the hell out of me.

365
35:11.980 --> 35:14.438
I think someone's sneaking around in here. Check over there.

366
35:14.521 --> 35:15.355
Let's go.

367
35:18.688 --> 35:20.230
-Let's go out this door. -Okay.

368
35:20.313 --> 35:21.355
-Let's go. -Quietly.

369
35:22.146 --> 35:23.271
Follow me.

370
35:46.646 --> 35:48.605
Hey, no one's here. Go check the back.

371
35:48.688 --> 35:49.646
We should hurry.

372
35:54.980 --> 35:57.396
Hey! Come out, asshole!

373
35:57.480 --> 35:59.605
If you don't, I'll blow your head off!

374
36:00.938 --> 36:03.063
Who's there? Come out!

375
36:03.563 --> 36:05.230
Hey! Over there!

376
36:06.438 --> 36:07.563
Come out!

377
36:13.480 --> 36:14.688
Hey, over there.

378
36:24.063 --> 36:25.188
What was that?

379
36:44.771 --> 36:47.438
-Hey, what was that? -Where?

380
36:58.813 --> 37:00.563
They're gone. Let's go.

381
37:01.313 --> 37:02.188
Hurry.

382
38:35.271 --> 38:36.188
Watch out.

383
39:00.230 --> 39:01.438
I'm sorry.

384
39:02.021 --> 39:04.271
I made you break the law and it got dangerous too.

385
39:08.980 --> 39:10.230
I chose to do it.

386
39:11.563 --> 39:13.355
You didn't force me.

387
39:13.438 --> 39:14.521
Right?

388
39:23.230 --> 39:26.313
Let's hope Sak's DNA is in here.

389
39:26.938 --> 39:30.105
We can't use it as evidence, but it should help strengthen the case.

390
40:24.980 --> 40:26.646
I'm on my way back.

391
40:30.646 --> 40:35.271
You better find out…

392
40:37.438 --> 40:40.896
who dared to disrespect me.

393
40:41.688 --> 40:43.313
Whoever did that shit

394
40:43.980 --> 40:46.813
is disrespecting the spirits too.

395
41:36.813 --> 41:37.646
Damn it.

396
47:40.563 --> 47:45.563
Subtitle translation by: Parida Kim
